Package: plotplanner
Title: Generate 'ggplot2' Figure Code from an Excel Specification
Version: 0.0.2
Authors@R: person("ichirio", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "ichi.r.pro@gmail.com")
Description: Reads an Excel specification (plot type, ADaM variable roles,
    codelist selections, layer patterns and presets) and writes skeleton
    'ggplot2' code. The generated code depends only on 'ggplot2' and the
    relevant extension packages, not on 'plotplanner'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    openxlsx,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    dplyr,
    ggplot2 (>= 3.5.0),
    ggsurvfit,
    haven,
    patchwork,
    survival,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    tibble
Config/testthat/edition: 3
